  "text": "Movement of atoms inside solid materials happens faster along the interfaces between crystals and on exposed surfaces than through the bulk crystal lattice. To make it easier to study these faster pathways quantitatively, a set of equations was derived that treats diffusion along an interface in the same way as heat spreading through a very thin metal sheet that is placed inside a soft, insulating material. The resulting formula predicts how deep the atoms will penetrate over time when they travel along these interfaces. When the predictions were compared with measurements of self‑movement of atoms in a common metallic element, the calculated curves matched the observed data closely, confirming the usefulness of the approach."
